      "option": "T1",
      "label": "T1 · Ink dashes",
      "note": "PROPOSED. Short ink dashes along the line of fire, from the gun to where the round ended, on a paper halo so they read over forest and hatching. They sweep out in a tenth of a second, drift outward a little, thin toward the far end and fade over half a second. The simplest mark in the map's own material (ink): a dotted line, not a light. Seen on the board: it reads at every zoom and is the heaviest ink of the five, and a dashed line is already the planner's and the drop's mark.",
